+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+set -uo pipefail
+
+if (( $# < 2 )); then
+  echo "usage: $0 LABEL COMMAND [ARG ...]" >&2
+  exit 2
+fi
+
+label=$1
+shift
+log_dir=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)
+log_path="${log_dir}/${label}.log"
+
+{
+  printf 'COMMAND:'
+  printf ' %q' "$@"
+  printf '\n'
+  "$@"
+  status=$?
+  printf '\nEXIT_STATUS: %d\n' "$status"
+} >"$log_path" 2>&1
+
+exit "$status"

All seven audit stages are complete. REVIEW.md records a FAIL / NOT_LEGIT verdict based on machine-checked body-sensitivity and opposite-value false-conclusion witnesses; reviewer scripts, artifacts, and bounded logs are preserved under evidence/.
